# ── Local config that carries credentials ────────────────────────────
# `.mcp.json` USED to be ignored: a local dev copy holding live API keys was
# swept into a commit here by a careless `git add -A` on 2026-08-26, and only
# GitHub's push protection stopped it from being published. It is now tracked,
# because Grok Build reads a plugin's MCP servers from `.mcp.json` and the
# marketplace installs this repo directly. The ignore rule could not protect it
# anyway once tracked, so the guard moved into the test suite:
# test_committed_mcp_json_declares_only_this_server fails if anything but the
# yantrikdb entry appears there, or if it grows an `env` block.
# Put local dev servers in `.mcp.local.json`, or register them with
# `claude mcp add-json <name> <json> -s local`, which keeps them out of the repo.
.mcp.local.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.claude/
*.local.json

